course: dictionary
lesson: 11060
title: Weep: a deeper word for cry
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Weep means cry, but it is a more serious or old-fashioned word. You will meet it in stories, poems and the Bible. In everyday talk people say cry. When you see weep, the author is telling you that someone is deeply sad.
explain: Read this: «Peter went outside and wept bitterly.» The word bitterly is a clue. It tells you the crying was hard and full of pain, not a small sniff. The context helps you feel how strong the sadness is.
explain: Weep is not only about people. A wound can weep, which means it lets out a slow drip of liquid, like a tiny leak. The words around the word tell you which meaning fits.
explain: Weep can also show happy feelings. Weep for joy means crying because you are happy. So look at the clues around the word to decide whether the tears are sad or happy.
fact: Weep means to cry, letting tears fall, usually because you are sad.
fact: Weep is a more serious or old-fashioned word for cry; in everyday talk we say cry.
fact: The forms are weep, weeps, wept and weeping. «Wept» is the past form, as in «Jesus wept».
fact: A wound or surface can weep: it lets out a slow drip of liquid.
fact: Weep for joy means crying because you are happy.
exercise: «Peter went outside and wept bitterly.» What does wept mean here? | Laughed loudly at a joke | *Cried deeply because he was very sad | Ran outside to play | Slept soundly all night
exercise: A cut on Sam's knee keeps weeping a little liquid. What does weeping mean here? | Crying loudly at the doctor's | Singing a happy song | *Slowly dripping liquid | Growing bigger overnight
exercise: Mia says her sister wept for joy when she won the race. Why did she weep? | She was tired and sleepy | She was cold and wet | She was very angry | *She was very happy
test: Which word is the everyday word for weep? | *Cry | Shout | Sleep | Smile
test: «Jesus wept» comes at the tomb of his friend Lazarus, who had died. What does the context suggest? | Jesus was angry about the weather | *Jesus was deeply sad and grieving | Jesus was asleep | Jesus was laughing with his friends
exam: Which phrase means crying because you are happy? | Laugh out loud | Sleep in the rain | *Weep for joy | Weep with anger
